        <li class="style31">
          <div align="justify">Prof. Dr. <span id="lw_1260451447_0">Pirzada Qasim</span> Raza <span id="lw_1260451447_1">Siddiqui</span>, Vice Chancellor UoK, has expressed his grievances on the <span id="lw_1260451447_2">sudden death</span> of the famous young journalist Mr. <span id="lw_1260451447_3">Najeeb</span> Ahmed. He also condoled  the  death of Prof. Dr. Syed Abdul Qadeer, Former Founding Director, Area  Study Centre for Europe,  and said that he was an eminent scholar,  educationist and an excellent teacher. His death has left a void that  can never be fulfilled.&nbsp;&nbsp;</div>
        </li>
        <li class="style31">
          <div align="justify">Department of Visual Studies  is organizing the <strong><em>Thesis Exhibition</em></strong> of the Graduating Students of Visual Studies from December 13th to 15th 2009 at the STC building. Students of <span id="lw_1260451447_4">Industrial Design</span>, Graphic Design, <span id="lw_1260451447_5">Textile Design</span> and Fine Arts Departments will present their work. </div>
        </li>
        <li class="style31">
          <div align="justify">The Directorate of  Evening Program has announced that the date of admissions to  Masters Programs, B.S. &amp; Pharm-D and Certificate courses has been  extended up to <span id="lw_1260451447_4">Saturday, December 12th, 2009</span>. Forms are available from UBL Silver Jubilee gate (<span id="lw_1260451447_5">9:30 a.m. to 3:30 p.m</span>.) and at UBL Campus Branch (<span id="lw_1260451447_6">3:30pm to 7:30pm)</span> while completed forms are being received at the Directorate of Evening Program (3:30 pm to 7:30 pm). </div>
        </li>
        <li class="style31">
          <div align="justify">Registrar UoK,  Prof. <span id="lw_1260451447_7">Muhammad Rais</span> Alvi, has announced that the Board of Advanced Studies &amp; Research (BASR), <span id="lw_1260451447_8">University of Karachi</span> in its meeting held on 09th December 2009 under the chairmanship of Prof. Dr. <span id="lw_1260451447_9">Pirzada Qasim</span> Raza <span id="lw_1260451447_10">Siddiqui</span>,  Vice Chancellor UoK, awarded 5 M.Phil and 7 Ph.D. degrees in various  disciplines. Candidates who received M.Phil degrees include Mr. Bilal  A. Usmani (Mathematics), Ms.Sadia Majeed (Applied Economics), Ms. <span id="lw_1260451447_11">Shazia</span> Samar (Chemistry), Ms. Ghulam Fatima (Microbiology) and Ms. Mehwish  (Chemistry HEJ). Names of candidates who are awarded the Ph.D. degree  are Ms. Saeeda Bano (Biochemistry), Ms.Tayyaba <span id="lw_1260451447_12">Zarif</span> (Education), Ms. Shakeela A. Rehman (Geography), Mr. Shakir Hussain  Khan (Islamic Learning, Ms. Mahmooda Kazmi (Microbiology), Mr. Ansar  Ahmed (Urdu) and Ms. Afsheen Zehra - 10/12/09 </div>
        </li>
